Common TOPP options:
  -ini <file>                                                        Use the given TOPP INI file[96m[39m[95m[39m
  -log <file>                                                        Name of log file (created only when specified)[96m[39m[95m[39m
  -instance <n>                                                      Instance number for the TOPP INI file[96m (default: '1')[39m[95m[39m
  -debug <n>                                                         Sets the debug level[96m (default: '0')[39m[95m[39m
  -threads <n>                                                       Sets the number of threads allowed to be used by the TOPP tool (0 = all available cores)[96m (default: '1')[39m[95m[39m
  -write_ini <file>                                                  Writes the default configuration file[96m[39m[95m[39m
  -write_ctd <out_dir>                                               Writes the common tool description file(s) (Toolname(s).ctd) to <out_dir>[96m[39m[95m[39m
  -write_nested_cwl <out_dir>                                        Writes the Common Workflow Language file(s) (Toolname(s).cwl) to <out_dir>[96m[39m[95m[39m
  -write_cwl <out_dir>                                               Writes the Common Workflow Language file(s) (Toolname(s).cwl) to <out_dir>, but enforce a flat parameter hierarchy[96m[39m[95m[39m
  -write_nested_json <out_dir>                                       Writes the default configuration file[96m[39m[95m[39m
  -write_json <out_dir>                                              Writes the default configuration file, but compatible to the flat hierarchy[96m[39m[95m[39m
  -no_progress                                                       Disables progress logging to command line[96m[39m[95m[39m
  -force                                                             Overrides tool-specific checks[96m[39m[95m[39m
  -test                                                              Enables the test mode (needed for internal use only)[96m[39m[95m[39m
  --help                                                             Shows options[96m[39m[95m[39m
  --helphelp                                                         Shows all options (including advanced)[96m[39m[95m[39m

Algorithm section:
  -algorithm:write_debug                                             When debug mode is activated, several files with intermediate results are written to the folder 'debug' (do not use in parallel mode).[96m[39m[95m[39m

Settings for the calculation of a score indicating if a peak's intens
ity is significant in the local environment (between 0 and 1):
  -algorithm:intensity:bins <number>                                 Number of bins per dimension (RT and m/z). The higher this value, the more local the intensity significance score is.
This parameter should be decreased, if the algorithm is used on small regions of a map.[96m (default: '10')[39m[95m (min: '1')[39m

Settings for the calculation of a score indicating if a peak is part 
of a mass trace (between 0 and 1).:
  -algorithm:mass_trace:mz_tolerance <value>                         Tolerated m/z deviation of peaks belonging to the same mass trace.
It should be larger than the m/z resolution of the instrument.
This value must be smaller than that 1/charge_high![96m (default: '0.03')[39m[95m (min: '0.0')[39m
  -algorithm:mass_trace:min_spectra <number>                         Number of spectra that have to show a similar peak mass in a mass trace.[96m (default: '10')[39m[95m (min: '1')[39m
  -algorithm:mass_trace:max_missing <number>                         Number of consecutive spectra where a high mass deviation or missing peak is acceptable.
This parameter should be well below 'min_spectra'![96m (default: '1')[39m[95m (min: '0')[39m
  -algorithm:mass_trace:slope_bound <value>                          The maximum slope of mass trace intensities when extending from the highest peak.
This parameter is important to separate overlapping elution peaks.
It should be increased if feature elution profiles fluctuate a lot.[96m (default: '0.1')[39m[95m (min: '0.0')[39m

Settings for the calculation of a score indicating if a peak is part 
of a isotopic pattern (between 0 and 1).:
  -algorithm:isotopic_pattern:charge_low <number>                    Lowest charge to search for.[96m (default: '1')[39m[95m (min: '1')[39m
  -algorithm:isotopic_pattern:charge_high <number>                   Highest charge to search for.[96m (default: '4')[39m[95m (min: '1')[39m
  -algorithm:isotopic_pattern:mz_tolerance <value>                   Tolerated m/z deviation from the theoretical isotopic pattern.
It should be larger than the m/z resolution of the instrument.
This value must be smaller than that 1/charge_high![96m (default: '0.03')[39m[95m (min: '0.0')[39m
  -algorithm:isotopic_pattern:intensity_percentage <value>           Isotopic peaks that contribute more than this percentage to the overall isotope pattern intensity must be present.[96m (default: '10.0')[39m[95m (min: '0.0' max: '100.0')[39m
  -algorithm:isotopic_pattern:intensity_percentage_optional <value>  Isotopic peaks that contribute more than this percentage to the overall isotope pattern intensity can be missing.[96m (default: '0.1')[39m[95m (min: '0.0' max: '100.0')[39m
  -algorithm:isotopic_pattern:optional_fit_improvement <value>       Minimal percental improvement of isotope fit to allow leaving out an optional peak.[96m (default: '2.0')[39m[95m (min: '0.0' max: '100.0')[39m
  -algorithm:isotopic_pattern:mass_window_width <value>              Window width in Dalton for precalculation of estimated isotope distributions.[96m (default: '25.0')[39m[95m (min: '1.0' max: '200.0')[39m
  -algorithm:isotopic_pattern:abundance_12C <value>                  Rel. abundance of the light carbon. Modify if labeled.[96m (default: '98.930000000000007')[39m[95m (min: '0.0' max: '100.0')[39m
  -algorithm:isotopic_pattern:abundance_14N <value>                  Rel. abundance of the light nitrogen. Modify if labeled.[96m (default: '99.632000000000005')[39m[95m (min: '0.0' max: '100.0')[39m

Settings that determine which peaks are considered a seed:
  -algorithm:seed:min_score <value>                                  Minimum seed score a peak has to reach to be used as seed.
The seed score is the geometric mean of intensity score, mass trace score and isotope pattern score.
If your features show a large deviation from the averagene isotope distribution or from an gaussian elution profile, lower this score.[96m (default: '0.8')[39m[95m (min: '0.0' max: '1.0')[39m

Settings for the model fitting:
  -algorithm:fit:max_iterations <number>                             Maximum number of iterations of the fit.[96m (default: '500')[39m[95m (min: '1')[39m

Settings for the features (intensity, quality assessment, ...):
  -algorithm:feature:min_score <value>                               Feature score threshold for a feature to be reported.
The feature score is the geometric mean of the average relative deviation and the correlation between the model and the observed peaks.[96m (default: '0.7')[39m[95m (min: '0.0' max: '1.0')[39m
  -algorithm:feature:min_isotope_fit <value>                         Minimum isotope fit of the feature before model fitting.[96m (default: '0.8')[39m[95m (min: '0.0' max: '1.0')[39m
  -algorithm:feature:min_trace_score <value>                         Trace score threshold.
Traces below this threshold are removed after the model fitting.
This parameter is important for features that overlap in m/z dimension.[96m (default: '0.5')[39m[95m (min: '0.0' max: '1.0')[39m
  -algorithm:feature:min_rt_span <value>                             Minimum RT span in relation to extended area that has to remain after model fitting.[96m (default: '0.333')[39m[95m (min: '0.0' max: '1.0')[39m
  -algorithm:feature:max_rt_span <value>                             Maximum RT span in relation to extended area that the model is allowed to have.[96m (default: '2.5')[39m[95m (min: '0.5')[39m
  -algorithm:feature:rt_shape <choice>                               Choose model used for RT profile fitting. If set to symmetric a gauss shape is used, in case of asymmetric an EGH shape is used.[96m (default: 'symmetric')[39m[95m (valid: 'symmetric', 'asymmetric')[39m
  -algorithm:feature:max_intersection <value>                        Maximum allowed intersection of features.[96m (default: '0.35')[39m[95m (min: '0.0' max: '1.0')[39m
  -algorithm:feature:reported_mz <choice>                            The mass type that is reported for features.
'maximum' returns the m/z value of the highest mass trace.
'average' returns the intensity-weighted average m/z value of all contained peaks.
'monoisotopic' returns the monoisotopic m/z value derived from the fitted isotope model.[96m (default: 'monoisotopic')[39m[95m (valid: 'maximum', 'average', 'monoisotopic')[39m

Settings for user-specified seeds.:
  -algorithm:user-seed:rt_tolerance <value>                          Allowed RT deviation of seeds from the user-specified seed position.[96m (default: '5.0')[39m[95m (min: '0.0')[39m
  -algorithm:user-seed:mz_tolerance <value>                          Allowed m/z deviation of seeds from the user-specified seed position.[96m (default: '1.1')[39m[95m (min: '0.0')[39m
  -algorithm:user-seed:min_score <value>                             Overwrites 'seed:min_score' for user-specified seeds. The cutoff is typically a bit lower in this case.[96m (default: '0.5')[39m[95m (min: '0.0' max: '1.0')[39m

